AB  - Current life prediction methods of aero-engine have less degradation uncertainty analysis. Moreover, multiple correlation tasks with interpretability analysis are not studied deeply in the prediction process of entire life cycle. Therefore, this paper proposes a new remaining useful life (RUL) prediction approach based on multi-task learning with interpretability analysis. The change point of degradation data is obtained based on detection method in data preprocessing part. Then fault mode identification based on statistics-informed neural network (SINN), health index construction with contrastive learning, and RUL prediction based on cascade neural Turing machine (NTM) are handled based on multi-task learning. The convergence theorem of proposed approach is proved. A new multi-task pretrained algorithm is studied. Next, a novel multi-task weight optimization algorithm is developed. Two datasets of CMPASS and NCMPASS are utilized and experimental results show that: 1) Our approach has better point prediction, interval prediction, and life prediction performances than state-of-the-arts methods; 2) Proposed multi-task pretrained and weight optimization paradigm are better than traditional individual-task mode; 3) Ablation studies, model interpretability and correlation interpretability analysis results verify the effectiveness of proposed method.
