AB  - This paper proposes a novel decision support system (DSS) based on a new multi-criteria decision analysis (MCDA) method called Strong Sustainability Paradigm-based VlseKriterijumska Optimizacija I Kompromisno Resenje (SSP-VIKOR). The disadvantages of MCDA methods in existing decision support systems (DSSs), such as linear criteria compensation, have been raised by many researchers and practitioners. In this research paper, we undertake the challenge of developing a DSS based on the MCDA method, considering the modeling criteria of compensation reduction. The developed DSS contributes to the field of artificial intelligence applications and their employment in engineering. The proposed DSS can be applied to sustainability assessment in a wide range of fields that require consideration of levels of criterion compensation. The developed method was applied to the problem of evaluating 25 European countries and the United States of America against healthcare resilience in the context of a pandemic. Improvement of healthcare systems in terms of sustainable communities and resilient environments involves many aspects, including resilience to crises such as pandemics. Various attempts to measure the resilience of healthcare systems can be found in the literature. However, not all of them allow their evaluation with simultaneous consideration of multiple evaluation criteria, their relevance, and the modeling of compensation reduction following the strong sustainability paradigm. Considering the modeling level of compensation reduction of criteria demonstrated the analytical potential and superiority of the developed method compared with classical compensatory MCDA methods. The comparative analysis and benchmarking of the SSP-VIKOR demonstrated that the method provides robust and reliable results.
