KW  - Deep fuzzy model
KW  - Neural architecture search
KW  - Evolutionary optimization
KW  - Fuzzy inference modules
AB  - Manually designing an interpretable and high-precision deep fuzzy model usually requires a large amount of prior knowledge and repeated experimental validation, which is both time-consuming and labor-intensive. To address this challenging issue, inspired by neural architecture search, this paper innovatively proposes a general automatic architecture search and parameter optimization approach which can automatically execute the learning process for optimal configuration of the modules stacked deep fuzzy model. In this approach, a hierarchical automatic search algorithm is first constructed based on evolutionary optimization theory. Through intelligently searching for the number of first-level parallel fuzzy inference modules and their combinatorial subsets, the degree of freedom for horizontal scaling of the deep fuzzy architecture can be dynamically regulated. Meanwhile, the sliding windows which can optimize the spatial layout of fuzzy inference modules are adaptively selected with variable sizes, enabling flexible vertical expansion of the architecture. Subsequently, the research focuses on the collaborative optimization of the logical inference and internal structure of the stacked modules: On the one hand, the number of fuzzy rules, types of fuzzy membership functions, and values of regularization coefficient are automatically determined, which can relieve experts from the tedious trial-and-error process and improve the accuracy of generated model. On the other hand, the random initialization of fuzzy membership function parameters avoids the traditional iterative solution process and reduces the computational complexity. Finally, the proposed approach is validated on several datasets. Experimental results demonstrate that it can automatically generate reasonable model tailored to the dataset characteristics, with its prediction accuracy significantly outperforming that of popular automatic architecture search methods and manually-designed models.
