KW  - Hypersonic flight control
KW  - Adaptive fuzzy rule-based fuzzy logic system
KW  - Fault-tolerant control
KW  - Prescribed performance
AB  - Hypersonic flight vehicles operating in maneuvering scenarios are exposed to actuator fault risks and multiple uncertainties. To address these challenges, an adaptive fuzzy rule-based fuzzy logic system (AFR-FLS) is proposed, based on which a fuzzy fault-tolerant control scheme with prescribed performance constraints is developed. First, AFR-FLS is constructed under a standard fuzzy inference framework and Lyapunov stability theory. Compared with traditional FLS, it eliminates the dependence on deterministic rule bases; in contrast to existing data-driven FLS, it preserves the fuzzy inference structure while requiring fewer learning parameters. Second, a low-complexity robust fault-tolerant control scheme without back-stepping is constructed by integrating pure-feedback affine transformation and adaptive robust compensation. Furthermore, a prescribed-time performance function with a concise structure is introduced to explicitly enforce performance constraints, leading to enhanced transient response and steady-state accuracy. Finally, extensive numerical simulations are conducted to demonstrate the effectiveness and superiority of the proposed approach.
